Samvat 2082 proved to be a challenging period for the Indian stock market, marked by heightened volatility, persistent foreign selling, short-lived rebounds, and significant correction in the benchmark indices. Persistent international and domestic headwinds created ongoing strain on equity valuations, testing investor resilience despite the solid foundation of India's long-term economic expansion.
Key factors suppressing market confidence in Samvat 2082 included intensifying geopolitical conflicts, elevated crude oil prices, climbing global bond yields, a strengthening US dollar, and ongoing sell-offs by Foreign Institutional Investors (FIIs).
As a result, the key benchmark Nifty 50 index witnessed nearly 11 percent drop on year-to-date basis. The bearish sentiment extended beyond mega-cap stocks across the broader market.
As India prepares to celebrate Diwali this week, investors will welcome Samvat 2083 amid a challenging year for equities. Brokerage PL Capital’s Technical Research Desk has shared the stock picks for Diwali 2026. The report highlights 10 stocks selected based on technical indicators such as support levels, RSI reversals, breakout patterns, higher-low formations, and moving average support.
 1. Apollo Hospitals: Buy, Target Price Rs 9,800 - 10,400 | Stoploss at Rs 7,000 
The brokerage has set the target price for Apollo Hospitals in the range Rs 9,800 - 10,400 and a stoploss of Rs 7,000. It said the stock has recently witnessed a significant erosion from the Rs 9,050 zone and has shown signs of bottoming out near the 7,500 level with a significant revival visible to improve the outlook and expecting for further upward move in the coming days. “The RSI has corrected well and is currently well positioned near the oversold zone with indication of a positive trend reversal to signal a buy with much upside potential visible and can carry on with the positive move further ahead,” it added.
 2. DLF Ltd: Buy, Target Price Rs 860 - 960 | Stoploss at Rs 570 
PL Capital has pegged the target price for DLF in the range of Rs 860 – 960 with a stoploss at Rs 570. The stock has been in consolidation for quite some time, sustaining above the important 200EMA at the 623 level on the weekly chart & forming a higher bottom formation along with the VCP pattern in the daily chart. Currently having positive candle formation with volume participation to improve the bias, anticipating a further rise in the coming days. The RSI is well placed, and with a positive trend reversal indication having much upside potential visible, it can carry on with the positive move further ahead. With the chart technically looking good, we suggest buying the stock for the upside targets of 860 and 960 levels keeping the stop loss at the 570 level.
 3. GE Vernova T&D India: Buy, Target Price Rs 5,100 – 5,450 | Stoploss at Rs 3400 
The brokerage has a target price in the range Rs 5,100 – 5,450 with stoploss at Rs 3400. It said the stock after a good consolidation near the Rs 4,200 zone has recently slipped and has hit the low near Rs 3,550 zone thereafter, with a significant revival with volume participation visible has once again improved the outlook anticipating to carry on with the positive move further ahead in the coming days. “The RSI has arrived near the oversold zone and has indicated a positive trend reversal to signal a buy and with much upside potential visible, can gain significantly. With the chart technically well placed and looking attractive, we suggest buying the stock for the upside targets of Rs 5,100 and Rs 5,450 levels keeping the stop loss at the Rs 3,400 level,” the brokerage said.
 4. HBL Engineering Ltd: Target Price Rs 1000 - 1080 | Stoploss at Rs 670 
